    "body": "# PR type\n- [x] Bug Fix\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Document Updates\n- [ ] More Models or Datasets Support\n\n# PR information\n\nFixes #10395\n\nWhen `split_list(ori_list, num_shards, contiguous=True)` was called with `num_shards > len(ori_list)`, it relied on `np.linspace(0, len(ori_list), num_shards + 1, dtype=np.int64)` for slice indexing.\nBecause float truncation occurs when casting to `int64`, for `split_list([1, 2], 4, contiguous=True)`, the index list evaluates to `[0, 0, 1, 1, 2]`. This produced `[[], [1], [], [2]]`, causing Rank 0 (shard 0, typically master worker in distributed processing) to receive an empty list `[]` while items were scattered across subsequent ranks.\n\nThis PR replaces the linspace slicing in the contiguous path with standard balanced chunking using pure Python integer division (`divmod(len(ori_list), num_shards)`). This ensures:\n1. Extra remainder items are evenly distributed into the leading shards, matching `torch.chunk`, `np.array_split`, and `contiguous=False`.\n2. When `num_shards > len(ori_list)`, items are placed into shards `0` through `len(ori_list) - 1`, and trailing shards are empty `[]`.\n3. Added validation `if num_shards <= 0: raise ValueError(...)`.\n4. Avoids floating-point precision truncation artifacts on large lists and removes unnecessary numpy reliance in this basic list utility.\n\n## Experiment results\n\n- Before fix:\n  `split_list([1, 2], 4, contiguous=True)` returned `[[], [1], [], [2]]`\n- After fix:\n  `split_list([1, 2], 4, contiguous=True)` returns `[[1], [2], [], []]`\n- Unit tests:\n  Ran `python -m unittest -v tests/utils/test_split_list.py`:\n  - `test_contiguous_order ... ok`\n  - `test_empty_input ... ok`\n  - `test_invalid_num_shards ... ok`\n  - `test_more_shards_than_items ... ok`\n  - `test_round_robin_order ... ok`\n  - `test_round_robin_preserves_item_identity ... ok`\n  - `test_round_robin_preserves_mixed_types ... ok`\n  - `test_round_robin_preserves_ragged_lists ... ok`\n  All 8 tests passed in 0.002s.\n- Linter:\n  `ruff check tests/utils/test_split_list.py` passed with 0 errors.\n\n# Checklist\n\n- [x] I have linked the related issue above, if there is one.\n- [x] I have reviewed and understand every changed line, and I can explain how the change works and why it is correct.\n- [x] I have run the relevant tests or reproductions locally, and included the commands and results above (if applicable).\n- [x] I am responsible for the content of this PR, regardless of how it was produced.\n",
